{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a stitch task (#5605) from the cobbler code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement `cmd/df` (filesystem disk space usage reporting) covering only SRD srd106 requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, and R1.4. Two files must be created: `cmd/df/main.go` (implementation) and `cmd/df/df_test.go` (differential tests against the GNU `gdf` reference binary). The implementation must follow the project's execution constitution, go style constitution, shared protocols (SIGPIPE handling, differential testing, graceful skip), and package contracts.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: All cmd/ packages compare Go binary output against Homebrew GNU reference binary (gdf) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n   - **Filesystem enumeration**: Need to list mounted filesystems, get block counts, calculate usage percentages\n   - **Column alignment**: Right-aligned numeric columns, left-aligned text columns, per-column width maxima\n   - **Use% calculation**: `ceiling((total - available) * 100 / total)` when total > 0, dash \"-\" when total is 0\n   - **1024-byte block units**: Default output uses 1K-blocks\n   - **Pseudo-filesystem filtering**: Exclude filesystems with 0 total blocks by default\n   - **FILE argument mode**: Report filesystem containing specific files, with error handling for non-existent files\n   - **No git commands**: Git managed externally by orchestrator\n   - **Write-first strategy**: Write all files before building/testing, avoid incremental compile-fix loops\n   - **Function size limit**: 40 lines max per function (hard limit from execution constitution)\n   - **File size limit**: 500 lines per Go source file\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd106-df.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD for df utility with requirements R1-R4\n     - R1.1: Default listing - all mounted filesystems excluding pseudo-fs (0 total blocks), columns: Filesystem, 1K-blocks, Used, Available, Use%, Mounted on\n     - R1.2: Header line with exact GNU df column names, right-aligned numerics, left-aligned Filesystem/Mounted on\n     - R1.3: Use% = ceiling((total-available)*100/total), dash for total=0, right-aligned with \"%\" suffix\n     - R1.4: FILE arguments report containing filesystem, non-existent FILE → stderr diagnostic + continue\n     - R1.5: Column widths = per-column maxima across all rows including header (needed for alignment but technically not in task scope - however essential for matching GNU df output)\n     - Non-goals: --sync, --total, -P, --block-size, -k (accepted but no-op)\n     - Package imports: pkg/format, pkg/sys\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (PROVIDED in context)\n     - DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - RunDiffTests function signature\n     - BuildBinary compiles Go package and returns binary path\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (PROVIDED in context)\n     - InstallSIGPIPEHandler() - installs SIGPIPE handler for clean pipe exit\n   \n   - **pkg/format/humansize.go** (PROVIDED in context)\n     - HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string - not needed for R1.1-R1.4 but available\n   \n   - **cmd/df/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - df implementation with default output and FILE argument support\n   \n   - **cmd/df/df_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests against gdf reference binary\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call was made (reading the SRD file) before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the exact requirements for R1.1-R1.4\n   - Identified that the task scope is limited to R1.1-R1.4 (default output, headers, Use% calculation, FILE arguments) - NOT the full SRD which includes -h, -H, -T, -i, -a, -l, -t, -x, --output flags\n   - Need to determine how to enumerate mounted filesystems on macOS/Darwin (likely using `syscall.Statfs` or similar)\n   - R1.5 (column width alignment) is not explicitly in the task requirements but is essential for matching GNU df output and is closely related to R1.2\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: Extremely detailed stitch task prompt containing the full project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements R1.1-R1.4, design decisions D1-D4, acceptance criteria AC1-AC4, constraints, shared protocols, and package contracts. The role specified: \"You are a software engineer executing a single task from a work queue.\"\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/df/main.go` implementing srd106 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4\n   - Create `cmd/df/df_test.go` with differential tests against gdf\n   - Verify compilation with `go build ./cmd/df/`\n   - Verify tests pass with `go test ./cmd/df/ -count=1`\n   - Verify `go vet ./cmd/df/` reports no issues\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd106-df.yaml`) and was about to begin implementing the df utility. No code has been written yet. The next step was to plan the implementation approach and write both `cmd/df/main.go` and `cmd/df/df_test.go`.\n\n   Key implementation details gathered from the SRD:\n   - On macOS, need to use `unix.Getfsstat` or similar to enumerate mounted filesystems\n   - Each filesystem entry needs: device name, mount point, fs type, total blocks, free blocks, available blocks\n   - Default block size is 1024 bytes (1K-blocks)\n   - Use% uses ceiling division: `math.Ceil(float64(used) * 100 / float64(total))`\n   - Column alignment requires computing max width per column across all rows + header\n   - Pseudo-filesystems (total blocks = 0) are excluded by default\n   - FILE arguments use `syscall.Statfs` to find the containing filesystem\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement `cmd/df/main.go` and `cmd/df/df_test.go` per the task description. The task states: \"Implement srd106 requirement R1.1 per the SRD\", \"Implement srd106 requirement R1.2 per the SRD\", \"Implement srd106 requirement R1.3 per the SRD\", \"Implement srd106 requirement R1.4 per the SRD\". \n\n   The implementation needs to:\n   1. Use `golang.org/x/sys/unix` to enumerate mounted filesystems (Getfsstat on Darwin)\n   2. Calculate sizes in 1K-blocks, compute Use% with ceiling division\n   3. Format output with proper column alignment matching GNU df\n   4. Handle FILE arguments by stat-ing files to find their containing filesystem\n   5. Write differential tests comparing output against `gdf` reference binary\n   6. Follow the write-first strategy: write all code, then build and test once\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5605/e6b56990-b444-4142-be23-d97fbc698916.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b56990-b444-4142-be23-d97fbc698916","uuid":"f58291c0-60d8-4546-9850-1d0c7a9c7cc5","timestamp":"2026-05-27T19:03:55.978Z","isSynthetic":true}
