{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PbBzHLRUreWgSxd4pC826B","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive report with all the findings:\n\n## Comprehensive Analysis of Go Unix Utils Project Structure\n\nI've thoroughly explored the go-unix-utils project and gathered all requested information. Here's a complete breakdown:\n\n### 1. SIGPIPE Handler Signature\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5605/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n```\n\nThis function installs a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to exit with code 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching GNU coreutils behavior. It uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel and spawns a goroutine to listen for the signal. It's safe to call multiple times.\n\n### 2. DiffTest Structure and RunDiffTests Signature\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5605/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string\n    Args          []string\n    Stdin         []byte\n    Env           []string\n    WorkDir       string\n    ExitCode      int\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n```\n\nKey design patterns:\n- `Stdin: nil` means both binaries receive EOF immediately\n- `Env: nil` means inherit test process environment with `LC_ALL=C` applied\n- `Normalize` holds a slice of normalization functions applied in order\n- `ExpectedFiles` can validate created files\n- Includes `TimestampNormalizer` and `ComposeNormalizers` utilities\n\n### 3. Example Cmd Implementations with Differential Testing\n\n**Simple Example - cmd/echo:**\n\nMain features:\n- Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at startup\n- Flag parsing with early exit on unrecognized flags\n- Escape sequence interpretation with `-e` flag\n- Uses `os.Stdout.WriteString()` for output\n\nTest pattern: `echo_test.go` uses `testutils.RunDiffTests()` with reference binary `gecho`, testing ~50 cases covering flag combinations, escape sequences, and edge cases.\n\n**Another Example - cmd/true:**\n\nMain features:\n- Minimal implementation (43 lines)\n- Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n- Handles `--help` and `--version` flags\n- Ignores all other arguments\n\n**cmd/yes:**\n\nMain features:\n- Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n- Implements efficient block-based output for high performance\n- Manual EPIPE detection with `errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE)`\n- Two test approaches: differential tests with `RunDiffTests()` and custom SIGPIPE tests\n\n### 4. Go Module Dependencies\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5605/go.mod`\n\n```\nmodule github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils\n\ngo 1.26.3\n\nreplace github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils => ./\n\nrequire golang.org/x/sys v0.45.0\nrequire golang.org/x/crypto v0.52.0\n```\n\nYes, `golang.org/x/sys/unix` is imported (particularly in `pkg/sys/terminal.go` for IOCTL operations).\n\n### 5. Filesystem Functions in pkg/sys/\n**Available files:**\n- `sigpipe.go` - SIGPIPE handler (see #1)\n- `fileinfo.go` - Extended file metadata\n- `stat_darwin.go` - Darwin-specific stat operations\n- `terminal.go` - Terminal width detection\n- `signal.go` - Terminal resize signal handling\n\n**Key FileInfo functions:**\n\n```go\ntype FileInfo struct {\n    Mode       os.FileMode\n    Size       int64\n    Nlink      uint64\n    Uid        uint32\n    Gid        uint32\n    Rdev       uint64\n    Dev        uint64\n    Ino        uint64\n    Blocks     int64\n    Blksize    int64\n    ModTime    time.Time\n    AccessTime time.Time\n    ChangeTime time.Time\n    Info       os.FileInfo\n}\n\nfunc Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\nfunc Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\n```\n\n**Terminal functions:**\n- `TerminalWidth() (int, error)` - Uses `unix.IoctlGetWinsize()`\n- `IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool` - Checks if fd is a terminal\n- `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` - Registers SIGWINCH handlers\n\n**Note:** No getfsstat/statfs/mount info functions are present in this project.\n\n### 6. Format Package Functions\n**Files available:**\n- `humansize.go` - Human-readable byte formatting\n- `pad.go` - String padding utilities\n- `color.go` - ANSI color output for file types\n- `columns.go` - Multi-column grid layout\n- `color_test.go`, `humansize_test.go`, `pad_test.go` - Tests\n\n**Key functions:**\n\n```go\n// Human-readable size with binary/SI unit selection\nfunc HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string\n\n// String padding\nfunc PadRight(s string, width int) string\nfunc PadLeft(s string, width int) string\n\n// Column layout\nfunc Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string\n\n// ANSI color utilities\nfunc FileTypeColor(mode os.FileMode) string\nfunc Reset() string\nfunc ColorEnabled(w io.Writer) bool\nfunc SetColorEnabled(enabled bool)\n```\n\n### 7. Testing Infrastructure Pattern\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5605/pkg/testutils/build.go`\n\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n```\n\nThis helper:\n- Compiles the Go package at `dir`\n- Returns the binary path\n- Cleans up via `t.TempDir()`\n- Fatal on build failure\n\n### Pattern Summary\n\nAll cmd implementations follow this pattern:\n1. `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` as first operation in main\n2. Parse arguments and flags\n3. Validate and execute core logic\n4. Use `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...)` for error messages\n5. Call `os.Exit(exitCode)` when needed\n\nTest files follow the differential testing pattern:\n1. Build the Go binary with `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n2. Look up reference binary (e.g., `gcat`, `gecho`, `gyes`)\n3. Define test cases as `[]testutils.DiffTest`\n4. Call `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)`\n5. Add custom integration tests for SIGPIPE, file I/O, etc."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b56990-b444-4142-be23-d97fbc698916","uuid":"e8d81f98-532d-41d5-ba60-0711849dc643","timestamp":"2026-05-27T19:04:56.594Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the patterns used in this Go project for implementing cmd/ utilities. Please find and show me:\n\n1. The full contents of `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` - I need the SIGPIPE handler signature\n2. The full contents of `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` - I need the DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests signature\n3. Any existing cmd/ implementation that uses differential testing (look for a simple one like cmd/cat or cmd/echo or cmd/yes) - show me the main.go and the test file so I can follow the same patterns\n4. Check if `golang.org/x/sys/unix` is in go.mod\n5. Look at `pkg/sys/` for any filesystem-related functions (statfs, getfsstat, mount info)\n6. Look at `pkg/format/` for any relevant formatting functions\n\nSearch breadth: very thorough","agentId":"a0afa48c652004c71","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive report with all the findings:\n\n## Comprehensive Analysis of Go Unix Utils Project Structure\n\nI've thoroughly explored the go-unix-utils project and gathered all requested information. Here's a complete breakdown:\n\n### 1. SIGPIPE Handler Signature\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5605/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n```\n\nThis function installs a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to exit with code 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching GNU coreutils behavior. It uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel and spawns a goroutine to listen for the signal. It's safe to call multiple times.\n\n### 2. DiffTest