thub.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils\n\ngo 1.26.3\n\nreplace github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils => ./\n\nrequire golang.org/x/sys v0.45.0\nrequire golang.org/x/crypto v0.52.0\n```\n\nYes, `golang.org/x/sys/unix` is imported (particularly in `pkg/sys/terminal.go` for IOCTL operations).\n\n### 5. Filesystem Functions in pkg/sys/\n**Available files:**\n- `sigpipe.go` - SIGPIPE handler (see #1)\n- `fileinfo.go` - Extended file metadata\n- `stat_darwin.go` - Darwin-specific stat operations\n- `terminal.go` - Terminal width detection\n- `signal.go` - Terminal resize signal handling\n\n**Key FileInfo functions:**\n\n```go\ntype FileInfo struct {\n    Mode       os.FileMode\n    Size       int64\n    Nlink      uint64\n    Uid        uint32\n    Gid        uint32\n    Rdev       uint64\n    Dev        uint64\n    Ino        uint64\n    Blocks     int64\n    Blksize    int64\n    ModTime    time.Time\n    AccessTime time.Time\n    ChangeTime time.Time\n    Info       os.FileInfo\n}\n\nfunc Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\nfunc Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\n```\n\n**Terminal functions:**\n- `TerminalWidth() (int, error)` - Uses `unix.IoctlGetWinsize()`\n- `IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool` - Checks if fd is a terminal\n- `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` - Registers SIGWINCH handlers\n\n**Note:** No getfsstat/statfs/mount info functions are present in this project.\n\n### 6. Format Package Functions\n**Files available:**\n- `humansize.go` - Human-readable byte formatting\n- `pad.go` - String padding utilities\n- `color.go` - ANSI color output for file types\n- `columns.go` - Multi-column grid layout\n- `color_test.go`, `humansize_test.go`, `pad_test.go` - Tests\n\n**Key functions:**\n\n```go\n// Human-readable size with binary/SI unit selection\nfunc HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string\n\n// String padding\nfunc PadRight(s string, width int) string\nfunc PadLeft(s string, width int) string\n\n// Column layout\nfunc Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string\n\n// ANSI color utilities\nfunc FileTypeColor(mode os.FileMode) string\nfunc Reset() string\nfunc ColorEnabled(w io.Writer) bool\nfunc SetColorEnabled(enabled bool)\n```\n\n### 7. Testing Infrastructure Pattern\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5605/pkg/testutils/build.go`\n\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n```\n\nThis helper:\n- Compiles the Go package at `dir`\n- Returns the binary path\n- Cleans up via `t.TempDir()`\n- Fatal on build failure\n\n### Pattern Summary\n\nAll cmd implementations follow this pattern:\n1. `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` as first operation in main\n2. Parse arguments and flags\n3. Validate and execute core logic\n4. Use `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...)` for error messages\n5. Call `os.Exit(exitCode)` when needed\n\nTest files follow the differential testing pattern:\n1. Build the Go binary with `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n2. Look up reference binary (e.g., `gcat`, `gecho`, `gyes`)\n3. Define test cases as `[]testutils.DiffTest`\n4. Call `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)`\n5. Add custom integration tests for SIGPIPE, file I/O, etc."}],"totalDurationMs":48878,"totalTokens":48627,"totalToolUseCount":39,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2536,"cache_read_input_tokens":44243,"output_tokens":1841,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2536},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":7,"output_tokens":1841,"cache_read_input_tokens":44243,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2536,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":19,"searchCount":6,"bashCount":14,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
